1
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:35,540
Oh, Neref, I shall savor killing you.

2
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:40,340
To avenge my dear son, I shall rip
out your insides while you watch.

3
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:45,160
And I can't let him find Whole Horse's
body or else my chance will be lost.

4
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:47,458
She's not behind the counter either.

5
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,485
It'll be even worse if
the other three show up.

6
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:53,080
I need to kill them one by one, damn it.

7
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,500
Stay back. Go away.

8
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,700
Oh, madame, are you here?

9
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:02,660
I thought I heard some kind of
crash back here. Are you okay?

10
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:10,360
I'm coming in, madame.

11
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:16,880
Oh, no! What happened?

12
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,300
Oh, it's nothing.

13
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,180
It's only a tiny fall.

14
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,301
Just bruised my hip a little bit.

15
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:24,980
You fell down?

16
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,377
You can't be falling now.

17
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:27,957
And you burned your left hand?

18
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,216
You're being much, much too careless.

19
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,820
Oh, thank you, dear boy. I'm fine.

20
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,680
No problem, I promise.

21
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,152
Who said you could come in here, damn it!

22
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:52,920
I'll spare you my wrath for
now, But when the time is right,

23
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,217
I'll kill you just like I
killed that bastard hole-horse.

24
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:00,241
All it takes is just a tiny little
wound, and then you're finished.

25
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,282
I'll turn you into my very
own puppet of justice!

26
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:08,750
Cool.

27
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:09,663
Here, your staff.

28
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,340
Madame, you seem to be
sweating a lot. It's nothing.

29
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:14,897
Don't concern yourself with me.

30
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:15,810
I'm fine.

31
00:03:15,893 --> 00:03:17,977
Just go to your room and get some rest.

32
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:19,280
Well, if you insist.

33
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,437
So, I was wondering, are you running
the entire hotel all by yourself?

34
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:26,020
Don't you have some family around to help?

35
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,360
Like a son?

36
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:29,920
I've gotten used to living alone.

37
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,060
Ah, I see.

38
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,900
Sounds lonely to me.

39
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:37,104
Just think, life with a
son and daughter-in-law.

40
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:40,277
Your grandkids could run
around and play in the lobby.

41
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,417
They'd definitely cheer this place up.

42
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:46,088
It'd be a little noisy, but
that's what makes families great!

43
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:51,397
If you had a son, he'd probably
be older than me, right?

44
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,777
Hey, what's the matter?

45
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:55,625
Did you have a son who
moved away or something?

46
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,757
No, he passed away.

47
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,500
Oh, I'm so sorry.

48
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,898
That was terribly insensitive of me.

49
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,157
You're the one who
killed him, you monster.

50
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,600
I despise you.

51
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,200
I'll slaughter you.

52
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,640
I'll slaughter you.

53
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,340
Please sit down.

54
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,497
I was still just a kid.

55
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:16,700
Isn't this great?

56
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:17,977
Ah, the memories.

57
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:22,940
Tonight you can think about me
as if I'm your own beloved son

58
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,620
Ask me for anything, okay?

59
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,320
You rotten little brat!

60
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:32,280
I should just kill you
right now, you fool!

61
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:36,420
Wow, your living alone has
been pretty tough on you

62
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,650
Huh?

63
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:47,977
What's that guy doing there?

64
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:50,897
This Card must have made his stand vanish

65
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:54,680
as soon as it shot the bullet
into his mouth! Gah! What?

66
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,980
No, that face!

67
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:57,890
Hey!

68
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,687
Look behind you, Paula Raff!

69
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,120
Behind you, you fool!

70
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:02,640
No way!

71
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:03,978
You're whole horse!

72
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:05,877
What are you doing?

73
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,195
Getting my vengeance!

74
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:11,535
I'm the mother of Cenderfold who you
mercilessly murdered in cold blood!

75
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,870
Chariot!

76
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,777
So you're a stand-user all along!

77
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:24,060
Dare play a part in murdering my boy
and I'll make sure you pay for it!

78
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:25,870
Mr.

79
00:05:25,953 --> 00:05:26,915
Joestar, I need help!

80
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:28,900
It's too late.

81
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:33,061
I'm afraid your trusty friends will
never hear your cries, my dear.

82
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:34,950
Because...

83
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,340
I've summoned my own allies.

84
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:42,180
Who the hell are you guys?

85
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,380
Wait, it's you!

86
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:47,980
But you're dead!

87
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,024
You were dead when we got here!

88
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,749
You're the one from India!

89
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,060
Holy shit, we've got zombies!

90
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:09,360
Behold the terrifying
power of justice, my stand!

91
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:11,717
One can only have one stand,

92
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:16,800
But Justice the Fog Stand can transform
the dead into my personal army!

93
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:22,200
It can control hundreds of
corpses, even thousands of them!

94
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,777
She'll turn you into a personal puppet!

95
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,917
I need only to give you a little scratch.

96
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,717
It doesn't take much, you know.

97
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,020
Soon you'll be mine.

98
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:34,220
Then my Stand Justice will
take care of the rest!

99
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:36,820
You're dead! Yahoo!

100
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,937
I'm out of here!

101
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:42,160
Ah, ah, ah, Polnareff!

102
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:43,560
Don't I save you.

103
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,057
You're on your own, pal.

104
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:48,180
You can't escape my righteous
vengeance, Polnareff!

105
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,557
I'll yank your brains out
through your nostrils!

106
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:53,497
I'll snap your spine in
half and shatter your bones!

107
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,517
I'll crush your balls till they pop!

108
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,100
My vengeance comes now!

109
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:59,142
I couldn't possibly run so fast!

110
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,240
Take this!

111
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,270
Dammit!

112
00:07:04,353 --> 00:07:06,457
That filthy coward ran into the back room!

113
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:07,775
After him, you fools!

114
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,700
Break down that door at once!

115
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:15,760
Mare, just my luck.

116
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:18,333
This hallway leads down to the basement.

117
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:21,080
I'm so far away from them now. Mr.

118
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,417
Joestar and the others will never hear me.

119
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,697
I don't think those creepy
zombies can beat me,

120
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:29,015
but if I get even a single
scratch, I'll be in trouble.

121
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:32,065
She'll take control of
me just like Hall Horse.

122
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,070
Damn it!

123
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,967
Isn't there any way outside?

124
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:39,562
And of course the windows
have iron bars on them.

125
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,590
Damn it!

126
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:50,578
I just have to keep these freaks as
far away from my skin as possible.

127
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,113
And now they're coming down the hallway.

128
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,960
They must be checking every room. Damn it.

129
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,180
They're getting closer and closer.

130
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,300
Wait a minute. Oh, come on.

131
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:04,302
Did I run into another bathroom?

132
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:07,880
Why am I always getting
ambushed in bathrooms?

133
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,570
Damn it.

134
00:08:09,653 --> 00:08:11,460
The toilet is so dirty.

135
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,160
All right, just try it.

136
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:19,320
But the second you walk in, my chariot will
chop up four of you in a single breath.

137
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,960
What's going on?

138
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:38,060
Now it's totally quiet out there. Creepy.

139
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,340
Damn zombie.

140
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:45,900
That old hag what the hell are they doing
aren't they going to break down the door?

141
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:58,140
What's taking them so long
come on do something damn it!

142
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:12,590
Perfect!

143
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:17,860
You've finally fallen under my justice's
control, you shitty little brat!

144
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:24,980
And now, if you don't open that door
and come out on your own this second,

145
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:29,299
I'm going to slowly crush your face
and pull you through the keyhole!

146
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,480
Laugh now!

147
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:42,640
How pitiful, Polnareff.

148
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,480
Very pitiful, indeed.

149
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:53,611
This isn't even close to the level of
torture you put my centerfold through.

150
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:58,040
Because of your cowardice, my precious
son died in unimaginable agony.

151
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:03,660
Now then, how about we have
you clean the bathroom, eh?

152
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,160
Sound like a plan to you?

153
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:18,940
Lick the toilet until
it sparkles like noob.

154
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,680
Don't be shy.

155
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:24,240
Lick it till it's shiny, like this.

156
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:36,957
No, not that!

157
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,940
I'm not anything but that!

158
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:54,100
Oh, God, help me!

159
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:04,617
Oh, you startled me.

160
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:07,260
You must learn to knock, my young man.

161
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:09,600
What can I do for you?

162
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:14,020
I'm here looking for
Polnareff, and I did knock.

163
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:17,957
Maybe you didn't hear me because you
were too busy doing something else.

164
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,380
I wonder what.

165
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:31,980
I'm looking for Polnareff,
but I can't find him.

166
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:33,420
Seen him, Grandma?

167
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:34,870
Hmm, damn.

168
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:36,000
Now what?

169
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:37,980
Unlike Polnareff,

170
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:42,517
this Jotaro is clever and knows the right
questions to ask to get what he wants.

171
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,920
I have to be careful.

172
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,697
Playing dumb will just
make him more suspicious.

173
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:48,480
I need something else.

174
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:51,000
What a troublesome brat.

175
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:52,360
I know.

176
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,557
I'll tell him where he can find Polnareff,

177
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:58,917
and as soon as he turns his back, I'll
turn him into a pincushion with these.

178
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,040
Then he'll be easy
pickings for my justice.

179
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:05,420
Yes, of course I can help you.

180
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:08,160
I know exactly where he is, Mr. Jotaro.

181
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:11,660
He and I were just
having a lovely chat. Oh.

182
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:17,900
This isn't good.

183
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,740
Jotaro has no idea.

184
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,100
A tiny scratch will spell his doom.

185
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,400
Stay back. Tell Mr.

186
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:27,480
Joestar and Kakyoin that hag is the enemy.

187
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:32,260
He's in the bathroom, but he's
been in there for quite some time.

188
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,160
Of course he's taking a shit.

189
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,957
Through this door here?

190
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,280
Yes, that's right.

191
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:44,957
Once you're through the
door, make a left turn.

192
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,700
The bathroom is at the
very end of the hall.

193
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:51,240
What an incompetent fool!

194
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,420
You are a child after all!

195
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:56,760
Murdering Polnareff will
delight my son's soul!

196
00:12:57,020 --> 00:13:01,837
And spilling your blood, Jotaro, will
send Lord Dio in Egypt into jubilation!

197
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,560
Oh, yeah, I forgot.

198
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,099
You have a second?

199
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,540
I got a question.

200
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:11,750
Huh?

201
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:12,663
What's the matter?

202
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:15,311
Did you trip or were you just that clumsy?

203
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,008
You should be more careful.

204
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,880
That was too close.

205
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:22,117
Yeah, could have been real bad.

206
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:26,317
It could have gone into your eye or cut
a huge chunk out of your scrawny neck.

207
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,920
You're pretty damn lucky.

208
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:34,080
Sorry to ask before you even get
up, but I have a few more questions

209
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,656
First on the list, how did
you know my name is Jotaro?

210
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,517
I never told you my name.

211
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,440
No one has, not since we got here.

212
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,900
I find that strange.

213
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,340
Well, come on, tell me.

214
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:49,817
You know, it's funny.

215
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:52,157
Maybe it's because I
watched Columbo as a kid.

216
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,877
But it's little details like
that that keep me up at night.

217
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:58,136
Oh, you're beginning to hurt
this old lady's feelings.

218
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,020
It's the guest book.

219
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:02,677
You wrote your name in
the guest book earlier.

220
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,701
Don't tell me you don't remember.

221
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:07,120
It's so dry.

222
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,660
You wrote Jotaro Kujo, yes.

223
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:14,960
Oh, then I guess you mean
this guest book here?

224
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:16,580
Yes, that's it.

225
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,980
See, your name is right here.

226
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,460
Jotaro Kujo?

227
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,265
Jotaro isn't ridden
anywhere in this old thing.

228
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:30,677
Calling me Joestar when we first
met was your first mistake.

229
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,231
I've suspected you since.

230
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:34,737
I told the others not to use my name.

231
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:36,460
And yet, you know it.

232
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,380
Which could only mean...

233
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,320
Cut the crap, you old hag!

234
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:46,317
I already know you're one of
the stand users that's after us.

235
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,230
The jig is up.

236
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,480
What's the matter now?

237
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,862
Aren't you going to show
me your stand and fight?

238
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,120
You're looking right at it!

239
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:15,540
whoa, whoa!

240
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:28,040
My stand justice always prevails!

241
00:15:28,380 --> 00:15:33,140
All it needs is one small scratch, and
then your life is as good as forfeit.

242
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:36,180
You've fallen into my trap, Jotaro!

243
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,400
Pull the riff!

244
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,197
Jotaro, it's me!

245
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,574
Whole Horse, remember?

246
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:46,328
The Yabba stand is made
entirely out of fog.

247
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:49,577
It'll split your wound right open
and start flowing through your body.

248
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:51,157
That's how she controls you with it.

249
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,920
It'll even control corpses.

250
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,800
Shut your mouth, Whole Horse!

251
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:07,020
Can you punch the fog with your fist?

252
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:08,737
Or cut the fog with your sword?

253
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:09,737
Or shoot it with a gun?

254
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:10,977
I don't think so.

255
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:12,680
Absolutely futile!

256
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:16,644
There's nothing you can
do but accept your fate!

257
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:20,477
It's the biggest, toughest,
fiercest stand there is!

258
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:23,560
Ours are puny by comparison,
we're no match for it!

259
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,280
